Built a native Track B generator based on [Corollary 15 and Example 16 of the paper](https://arxiv.org/html/2506.24012v1).

Deliverables:

- [Generator module](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2506.24012/gen_2506_24012.py)
- [Self-test report](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2506.24012/selftest_report.json)
- [README](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2506.24012/README.md)
- [Bare transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2506.24012/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [Hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2506.24012/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [Placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2506.24012/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

Local gates pass:

- 16/16 planted witnesses verified.
- 0/200,000 structure-aware random guesses.
- Four attacks failed across 8/8 seeds.
- Reference Gaussian solver succeeded as expected at 89,884 operations per instance.
- Compact trace/half-trace route uses at most 110 field operations.
- Scaling and canonicalization checks pass.

The result is not yet shippable: all three `harden.py` runs received HTTP 403 `Key limit exceeded (total limit)`. Those errors were preserved and not misreported as oracle failures. No `REJECTED.md` was created because the family itself has not failed G, H, or V.

Please replenish or replace `OPENROUTER_API_KEY`; then I can rerun STEP 4 and finalize the measured oracle evidence.
